Looking at the tiling: the top row shows the room's width equals 2 tile lengths, while the second band shows the width equals 4 tile widths plus 1 tile length. So 2L = 4W + L, giving L = 4W = 4 m (since the tile width W = 1 m).

Following the vertical side: width (1) + two stacked horizontals (2) + a vertical tile length (4) + another vertical tile length (4) + width (1) = 12 m. Equivalently, the right edge is marked into 12 one‑metre segments.

\boxed{12}
